35
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:13,780
when we had to draw our conversation to

36
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:17,100
its conclusion. I do hope that we can

37
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:24,340
continue there. You see, one of the

38
00:02:24,980 --> 00:02:30,080
factors in death is the mind is

39
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:35,180
so frightened. We are so frightened of that

40
00:02:35,180 --> 00:02:41,019
very word and nobody talks about it.

41
00:02:41,019 --> 00:02:46,859
I mean, it isn't a daily conversation. It

42
00:02:46,860 --> 00:02:49,360
is something to be avoided, something

43
00:02:49,360 --> 00:02:51,860
that is inevitable. For God's sake, keep

44
00:02:51,860 --> 00:02:54,500
it as far away as possible. We even paint

45
00:02:54,500 --> 00:02:57,140
corpses to make them look as though they're not there.

46
00:02:57,140 --> 00:03:02,260
That's the most absurd thing. Now, what

47
00:03:02,260 --> 00:03:07,380
we are discussing, sir, is, isn't it, the

48
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:13,479
understanding of death, its relation to

49
00:03:13,479 --> 00:03:19,579
living, and this thing called love. One

50
00:03:19,579 --> 00:03:23,479
cannot possibly understand the immensity, and

51
00:03:23,479 --> 00:03:27,380
it is immense, what this thing called

52
00:03:27,380 --> 00:03:33,140
death, unless there is real freedom from

53
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:38,900
fear. That's why we talked some time ago

54
00:03:38,900 --> 00:03:43,379
about the problem of fear. Without really

55
00:03:43,379 --> 00:03:47,859
freeing the mind, unless the mind frees

56
00:03:47,859 --> 00:03:51,879
itself from fear, there is no

57
00:03:51,879 --> 00:03:55,900
possibility of understanding the extraordinary beauty,

58
00:03:55,900 --> 00:03:59,020
strength and the vitality of death.

59
00:03:59,020 --> 00:04:05,420
A very, very remarkable way to put it, the vitality

60
00:04:05,420 --> 00:04:11,820
of death, and yet normally we regard it as the

61
00:04:11,820 --> 00:04:13,340
total negation of life.

62
00:04:13,340 --> 00:04:17,179
Right, that's right. So, I mean, if

63
00:04:17,179 --> 00:04:21,019
we are enquiring into this question of death,

64
00:04:21,019 --> 00:04:27,419
fear must be completely non-existent in us. Then I

65
00:04:27,419 --> 00:04:33,820
can proceed, then I can find out what death

66
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:37,899
means. We touched a little bit on

67
00:04:37,899 --> 00:04:41,979
reincarnation, the belief that is maintained throughout the

68
00:04:41,980 --> 00:04:47,780
East, which has no reality in daily life.

69
00:04:47,780 --> 00:04:53,580
It's like going to church every Sunday and being

70
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:59,780
mischievous for the rest of the six days.

71
00:04:59,780 --> 00:05:05,980
So, a person who is really serious, really attentive,

72
00:05:05,980 --> 00:05:09,020
goes into this question of death, he must

73
00:05:09,020 --> 00:05:12,060
understand what it means, the quality of it,

74
00:05:13,100 --> 00:05:15,460
not the ending of it. That's what

75
00:05:15,460 --> 00:05:17,820
we are going to discuss a little bit.

76
00:05:22,140 --> 00:05:27,260
The ancient Egyptians, the pharaohs and all the

77
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:32,380
first dynasty till the 18th and so on, they

78
00:05:32,780 --> 00:05:38,300
prepared for death. They said, we will cross that

79
00:05:38,300 --> 00:05:43,820
river with all our goods, with all our chariots,

80
00:05:43,820 --> 00:05:46,900
with all our belongings, with all our

81
00:05:46,900 --> 00:05:49,980
property, with all our... and therefore their caves,

82
00:05:49,980 --> 00:05:53,819
their tombs were filled with all the things

83
00:05:53,819 --> 00:05:57,659
of their daily life, corn, you know all that.

84
00:05:57,660 --> 00:06:03,540
So, living was only a means to ending dying.

85
00:06:03,540 --> 00:06:09,420
That's one way of looking at it. The other is

86
00:06:09,420 --> 00:06:13,860
reincarnation, which is the Indian-Asian outlook. And

87
00:06:13,860 --> 00:06:18,300
there is this whole idea of resurrection

88
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:22,140
of the Christians, reborn, carried by Gabriel Angelou

89
00:06:22,140 --> 00:06:25,740
and all that to heaven, and you would be...

90
00:06:29,740 --> 00:06:33,820
Now, what is the fact? These

91
00:06:33,820 --> 00:06:37,900
are all theories, suppositions, beliefs and non-facts.

92
00:06:37,900 --> 00:06:39,900
I mean, supposed to be born,

93
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,900
Jesus come out of the grave,

94
00:06:43,340 --> 00:06:46,620
resurrected physically. That is just a

95
00:06:46,620 --> 00:06:49,900
belief. There were no cameras then.

96
00:06:52,140 --> 00:06:55,580
There were no... ten people say, yes, I

97
00:06:55,580 --> 00:06:59,020
saw it. It's only seven people who saw it.

98
00:06:59,099 --> 00:07:00,299
There were no cameras then.

99
00:07:02,539 --> 00:07:06,059
There were no... ten people say, yes,

100
00:07:06,059 --> 00:07:09,580
I saw it. It's only somebody imagined.

101
00:07:13,099 --> 00:07:15,180
We'll go into that a little bit, a little later.

102
00:07:17,659 --> 00:07:22,619
So, there is this living and preparing for

103
00:07:22,619 --> 00:07:27,580
death, with the ancients, Egyptians, then there is the

104
00:07:27,580 --> 00:07:31,619
reincarnation, then there is resurrection. Now, if

105
00:07:31,619 --> 00:07:35,659
one isn't frightened, you follow, sir, deeply,

106
00:07:37,820 --> 00:07:43,500
then what is death? What is it that

107
00:07:43,500 --> 00:07:49,180
dies, apart from the organism? The organism may continue,

108
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:51,220
if you look after it very carefully,

109
00:07:51,220 --> 00:07:53,260
for eighty or ninety, a hundred years.

110
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:56,940
If you have no disease, if you have no

111
00:07:56,940 --> 00:08:00,620
accidents, if there is a way of living sanely,

112
00:08:01,580 --> 00:08:04,619
healthily, perhaps you'll last a hundred years or

113
00:08:04,619 --> 00:08:07,659
a hundred and ten years. And then what?

114
00:08:10,219 --> 00:08:14,699
You follow, sir? You live a hundred years.

115
00:08:14,699 --> 00:08:19,180
For what? For this kind of life? Fighting, quarrelling,

116
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:22,580
bickering, bitterness, anger, jealousy,

117
00:08:22,580 --> 00:08:25,980
futility, a meaningless existence.

118
00:08:27,740 --> 00:08:31,340
It is meaningless existence, as we are living now.

119
00:08:31,820 --> 00:08:34,140
A. And in terms of our previous

120
00:08:34,140 --> 00:08:36,460
remarks, this is all the content of consciousness.

121
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,820
K. Of consciousness. That's right. Now,

122
00:08:37,900 --> 00:08:40,620
this is all the content of consciousness.

123
00:08:40,620 --> 00:08:41,260
A. Of consciousness. That's right.

124
00:08:41,260 --> 00:08:41,740
Yes.

125
00:08:41,740 --> 00:08:46,100
K. Now, so, what is it that dies?

126
00:08:46,100 --> 00:08:50,460
And what is it one is frightened of?

127
00:08:52,780 --> 00:08:56,980
You follow? What is it one is frightened

128
00:08:56,980 --> 00:09:01,180
of? Death. Losing the known, losing my wife,

129
00:09:01,260 --> 00:09:03,499
losing my house, losing my

130
00:09:03,499 --> 00:09:05,739
– all the things I've acquired,

131
00:09:07,180 --> 00:09:11,900
losing this content of consciousness. You follow?

132
00:09:15,339 --> 00:09:23,420
So, can the content of consciousness be totally be emptied?

133
00:09:27,260 --> 00:09:27,979
You follow, sir?

134
00:09:27,979 --> 00:09:28,620
A. Yes, I do.

135
00:09:28,620 --> 00:09:35,500
K. Which is the living. The dying is the living.

136
00:09:37,500 --> 00:09:42,700
When the content is totally emptied.

137
00:09:48,140 --> 00:09:50,860
That means no attachment.

138
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:53,180
It is not a brutal cutting

139
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:55,500
off, but the understanding of attachment,

140
00:09:56,140 --> 00:09:58,860
the understanding of dependency,

141
00:09:58,860 --> 00:10:01,580
the understanding of acquisition,

142
00:10:01,580 --> 00:10:06,340
power, position, anxiety, all that. The

143
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:11,100
emptying of that is the real death.

144
00:10:11,100 --> 00:10:16,140
The emptying of that is the real death.

145
00:10:18,940 --> 00:10:22,860
And therefore, the emptying

146
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:26,780
of consciousness means the consciousness

147
00:10:26,780 --> 00:10:30,260
which has created its own limitation

148
00:10:30,260 --> 00:10:33,740
by its content comes to an end.

149
00:10:33,740 --> 00:10:35,420
I wonder if you...

150
00:10:35,420 --> 00:10:38,060
A. Yes, yes. Yes, you have.

151
00:10:38,060 --> 00:10:43,259
I was following you very carefully, and

152
00:10:43,259 --> 00:10:48,459
it occurred to me that there is

153
00:10:51,660 --> 00:10:57,660
a radical relation between birth and death, that the two,

154
00:10:59,500 --> 00:11:01,500
when they are looked upon

155
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:03,500
as moments in a total cycle,

156
00:11:04,460 --> 00:11:06,780
are not grasped at the depth level

157
00:11:06,780 --> 00:11:09,100
that you are beginning to speak about.

158
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:09,660
K. Yes, sir.

159
00:11:09,660 --> 00:11:10,700
A. Am I correct?

160
00:11:10,700 --> 00:11:11,100
K. That's correct.

161
00:11:11,100 --> 00:11:12,540
A. Good. Please, please do go on.

162
00:11:13,900 --> 00:11:18,740
K. So, death becomes a

163
00:11:18,740 --> 00:11:23,580
living when the content of consciousness,

164
00:11:25,020 --> 00:11:27,460
which makes its own frontier, its

165
00:11:27,460 --> 00:11:29,900
own limitation, comes to an end.

166
00:11:34,300 --> 00:11:38,220
And this is not a

167
00:11:38,220 --> 00:11:42,140
theory, not a speculative, intellectual grasp,

168
00:11:42,140 --> 00:11:47,100
but the actual perception of attachment.

169
00:11:47,100 --> 00:11:49,500
I am taking that as an example.

170
00:11:50,140 --> 00:11:54,780
Being attached to something, property, man, woman,

171
00:11:56,780 --> 00:11:58,860
the book I have written,

172
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:00,940
or the knowledge I have acquired,

173
00:12:00,940 --> 00:12:05,580
the attachment, and the battle to be detached,

174
00:12:07,020 --> 00:12:09,020
because attachment breeds pain.

175
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:12,060
Therefore I say to myself, I

176
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:14,060
must be detached, and the battle begins.

177
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:22,540
And the whole content of my consciousness is this,

178
00:12:23,260 --> 00:12:25,580
the battle which we described previously.

179
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:29,100
Now, can that content be detached?

180
00:12:29,100 --> 00:12:34,060
Now, can that content be emptied, empty itself?

181
00:12:35,500 --> 00:12:39,020
Not emptied by an act of perception.

182
00:12:41,580 --> 00:12:44,460
Empty itself, which means,

183
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:49,780
can this whole content be

184
00:12:49,780 --> 00:12:54,140
observed with its unconscious content?

185
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:55,900
You follow, sir?

186
00:12:56,700 --> 00:12:57,500
A. Yes, I do.

187
00:12:57,900 --> 00:13:00,140
K. There is consciousness.

188
00:13:00,140 --> 00:13:02,700
I can be consciously aware

189
00:13:02,700 --> 00:13:05,260
of the content of my consciousness.

190
00:13:06,140 --> 00:13:09,980
My house, my property, my wife, my children, my job,

191
00:13:11,580 --> 00:13:14,220
the things I have acquired, the things I have learnt,

192
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:16,300
I can be consciously aware of all that.

193
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:19,780
But also there is deeper content

194
00:13:19,780 --> 00:13:23,260
in the very recesses of my mind,

195
00:13:23,260 --> 00:13:29,500
which is racial, collective, acquired,

196
00:13:31,260 --> 00:13:35,900
the things that unconsciously I have gathered,

197
00:13:35,900 --> 00:13:37,900
the influences, the pressures, the

198
00:13:37,900 --> 00:13:39,900
strains of living in a world

199
00:13:39,900 --> 00:13:42,939
that is corrupt, all that is seeped in,

200
00:13:42,939 --> 00:13:45,420
all that is gathered in there.

201
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:49,500
A. Both personal and impersonal.

202
00:13:50,460 --> 00:13:53,260
Both personal and impersonal.

203
00:13:55,180 --> 00:13:58,140
This includes then what the depth psychologists are calling

204
00:13:58,140 --> 00:14:00,940
collective consciousness, as well

205
00:14:00,940 --> 00:14:03,740
as the personal consciousness.

206
00:14:03,740 --> 00:14:05,980
K. Collective as well as... So, that is that.

207
00:14:06,780 --> 00:14:09,500
Now, can all that be exposed?

208
00:14:11,660 --> 00:14:13,020
Because this is very important.

209
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:16,940
Because if I really want to go,

210
00:14:16,940 --> 00:14:20,540
if the mind really wants to understand and grasp

211
00:14:20,540 --> 00:14:22,780
the full meaning of death,

212
00:14:24,140 --> 00:14:26,260
the vastness of it, the great

213
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:28,380
quality of a mind that says,

214
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:34,380
yes, that's empty, gives a tremendous vitality, energy.

215
00:14:35,340 --> 00:14:42,300
So, my question is, can the mind be aware totally

216
00:14:43,820 --> 00:14:45,340
of all the content?

217
00:14:47,340 --> 00:14:48,460
As well as the open.

218
00:14:50,060 --> 00:14:55,580
The collective, the personal, the racial, the transitory.

219
00:14:56,860 --> 00:14:58,540
You follow? The whole of that.

220
00:15:01,100 --> 00:15:04,460
Now, we say it is possible through analysis.

221
00:15:07,260 --> 00:15:07,820
A. Yes, we do.

222
00:15:07,820 --> 00:15:11,100
K. I said analysis, paralysis.

223
00:15:11,100 --> 00:15:17,980
Because every analysis must be perfect, complete.

224
00:15:19,180 --> 00:15:21,340
And you are frightened that it may not be complete.

225
00:15:23,980 --> 00:15:26,180
And if you have not completed it,

226
00:15:26,180 --> 00:15:28,380
you carry it over as a memory,

227
00:15:29,180 --> 00:15:32,700
which will then analyse the next incident.

228
00:15:33,900 --> 00:15:37,340
So, each analysis brings its own incompleteness.

229
00:15:37,340 --> 00:15:40,060
Each analysis brings its own incompleteness.

230
00:15:41,340 --> 00:15:42,380
A. Oh, certainly, yes.

231
00:15:42,380 --> 00:15:44,940
K. Therefore it is a total paralysis.

232
00:15:48,540 --> 00:15:50,060
A. In following what you are saying,

233
00:15:51,180 --> 00:15:54,860
I am very taken with

234
00:15:54,860 --> 00:15:58,540
what we usually regard as death,

235
00:15:58,540 --> 00:16:00,500
which has a very clear

236
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,460
relationship to what you have said

237
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:06,380
about the endless series of analytical acts.

238
00:16:06,380 --> 00:16:07,100
K. Yes, sir.

239
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:09,740
A. We regard death as a

240
00:16:09,740 --> 00:16:11,820
terminus in terms of a line.

241
00:16:11,820 --> 00:16:15,100
K. Quite. Because we think laterally.

242
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:16,620
A. We think laterally, exactly.

243
00:16:16,620 --> 00:16:20,220
But what you are saying is, on the contrary,

244
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:23,980
we must regard this vertically.

245
00:16:25,180 --> 00:16:27,100
And in the regarding of it vertically,

246
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:31,100
we no longer see – please check

247
00:16:31,100 --> 00:16:32,940
me if I am off here –

248
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:40,540
we no longer see death as simply a moment

249
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:48,700
of termination to a certain trajectory of repetition.

250
00:16:51,260 --> 00:16:56,780
But there is a total qualitative change here,

251
00:16:56,780 --> 00:17:02,060
which is not the cessation of something

252
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:04,979
that we have to regret as

253
00:17:04,979 --> 00:17:06,859
though we had lost something valuable.

254
00:17:06,859 --> 00:17:08,940
K. Yes, I am leaving my wife and children,

255
00:17:09,740 --> 00:17:13,819
and my property, my blasted blank account.

256
00:17:17,099 --> 00:17:19,859
You see, sir, this is really – if

257
00:17:19,859 --> 00:17:22,619
one can go very deeply into this –

258
00:17:22,619 --> 00:17:28,379
there is this content, which is my consciousness,

259
00:17:29,739 --> 00:17:34,139
acquired, inherited, imposed, influenced,

260
00:17:34,139 --> 00:17:36,739
propaganda, attachment, detachment, anxiety,

261
00:17:36,739 --> 00:17:39,340
fear, pleasure, all that.

262
00:17:40,540 --> 00:17:42,939
And also the hidden things.

263
00:17:42,939 --> 00:17:50,060
I am asking myself, since analysis is really paralysis,

264
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:52,300
not intellectual supposition,

265
00:17:52,300 --> 00:17:55,740
but actually it is not a complete act.

266
00:17:57,260 --> 00:18:00,300
Analysis can never produce a complete act.

267
00:18:00,300 --> 00:18:03,260
The word analysis means to break

268
00:18:03,260 --> 00:18:06,220
up, you know, the breaking up.

269
00:18:06,220 --> 00:18:08,700
A. To loosen up. K. Loosen up, break up.

270
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:11,500
Therefore I reject that totally.

271
00:18:11,580 --> 00:18:15,660
I won't analyse, because I see the stupidity,

272
00:18:15,660 --> 00:18:18,860
the paralytic process of it.

273
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:22,140
Then what am I to do? You are following?

274
00:18:23,020 --> 00:18:27,100
Because that is the tradition, introspective,

275
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:31,820
or paralysis,

276
00:18:33,340 --> 00:18:36,380
or the way of life,

277
00:18:37,340 --> 00:18:45,740
or analysis by myself or by a professional,

278
00:18:46,460 --> 00:18:49,260
which is now the fact, and so on, so on.

279
00:18:49,980 --> 00:18:53,500
So, if the mind sees the truth of it,

280
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:56,540
and therefore analysis falls away,

281
00:18:56,540 --> 00:19:00,620
then what is the mind to do with the content?

282
00:19:01,580 --> 00:19:02,699
You...

283
00:19:04,860 --> 00:19:06,540
A. Yes, I do see that.

284
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:09,660
K. We know what the content is,

285
00:19:09,660 --> 00:19:11,500
we don't have it to be described.

286
00:19:12,939 --> 00:19:14,659
Now, what is it to

287
00:19:14,659 --> 00:19:16,379
do? It has to be emptied.

288
00:19:18,060 --> 00:19:20,459
Otherwise it is mere continuity.

289
00:19:21,659 --> 00:19:23,339
A. No, there is no

290
00:19:23,339 --> 00:19:25,020
use analysing what is already there,

291
00:19:25,020 --> 00:19:28,060
because that will not change what is there,

292
00:19:28,060 --> 00:19:30,060
in any way, shape or form.

293
00:19:31,260 --> 00:19:33,020
That seems to be very, very plain.

294
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:33,500
K. Plain.

295
00:19:33,500 --> 00:19:33,979
A. Although we...

296
00:19:36,219 --> 00:19:45,899
Perhaps you would, for a moment, explain why

297
00:19:48,540 --> 00:19:51,820
we simply refuse to see that.

298
00:19:51,820 --> 00:19:55,340
We do believe that an analytical enquiry

299
00:19:56,139 --> 00:19:58,219
is ordered to a revelation.

300
00:19:58,219 --> 00:20:00,300
K. No, sir, you can see it in a minute.

301
00:20:01,100 --> 00:20:05,739
Analysis implies the analyser and the analysed.

302
00:20:07,179 --> 00:20:09,500
The analyser is the analysed.

303
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:15,020
A. Yes, we are back to the observed word.

304
00:20:15,020 --> 00:20:16,699
K. Obviously. I am analysing my anger.

305
00:20:17,739 --> 00:20:19,100
Who is the analyser?

306
00:20:19,739 --> 00:20:22,459
Part of the fragment which is anger.

307
00:20:25,260 --> 00:20:28,459
So, the analyser pretends to be different.

308
00:20:30,860 --> 00:20:31,899
From the analysed.

309
00:20:32,620 --> 00:20:34,860
But when I see the truth

310
00:20:34,860 --> 00:20:37,100
that the analyser is the analysed,

311
00:20:37,739 --> 00:20:40,139
then a totally different action takes place.

312
00:20:42,300 --> 00:20:44,139
Then there is no conflict

313
00:20:44,139 --> 00:20:45,979
between the analyser and the analysed.

314
00:20:45,979 --> 00:20:49,500
There is instant action, a perception,

315
00:20:49,500 --> 00:20:52,620
which is the ending and going beyond the what is.

316
00:20:53,899 --> 00:20:56,699
A. The reason I asked for the explanation

317
00:20:56,700 --> 00:21:01,500
was because of the concern raised earlier about knowledge.

318
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:05,580
K. After all, the observer is knowledge.

319
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:09,260
A. Yes. I was concerned that

320
00:21:12,940 --> 00:21:19,420
study in its proper form was not regarded

321
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:23,580
in the context of our discussion as unprofitable as such.

322
00:21:24,700 --> 00:21:25,340
We don't mean that.

323
00:21:25,899 --> 00:21:27,419
We didn't even discuss that.

324
00:21:27,419 --> 00:21:28,699
K. Exactly. Yes, fine.

325
00:21:29,899 --> 00:21:33,020
Well, yes, it is obvious in terms of our discussion,

326
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:35,380
but the thing that concerns me

327
00:21:35,380 --> 00:21:37,740
is that so ingrained is the notion

328
00:21:38,620 --> 00:21:41,820
that, for instance, in the story I told about

329
00:21:41,820 --> 00:21:43,419
when I came to hear you years ago,

330
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:46,820
I began doing analysis while

331
00:21:46,820 --> 00:21:49,100
I was listening to your words

332
00:21:49,899 --> 00:21:52,699
and consequently I could hardly end up

333
00:21:52,699 --> 00:21:54,939
with anything qualitatively differently

334
00:21:54,940 --> 00:21:56,060
from what I came in with.

335
00:21:57,020 --> 00:21:59,500
But you see, I didn't see that at the time.

336
00:22:01,180 --> 00:22:04,300
In our videotaping, our conversations here,

337
00:22:05,100 --> 00:22:08,060
this will be listened to, and when we say yes,

338
00:22:08,620 --> 00:22:10,220
about knowledge, this is obvious,

339
00:22:10,220 --> 00:22:12,460
in the context of our conversation it is.

340
00:22:12,460 --> 00:22:13,340
But then I'm thinking...

341
00:22:13,340 --> 00:22:16,540
K. Not only in the context of our conversation,

342
00:22:16,540 --> 00:22:17,660
it is so. A. It is as such.

343
00:22:17,660 --> 00:22:18,540
K. Life is that.

344
00:22:18,540 --> 00:22:21,420
A. Exactly. I couldn't agree.

345
00:22:21,500 --> 00:22:25,740
But immediately I flashed back to my own behaviour

346
00:22:26,380 --> 00:22:31,660
and I know that I was not alone in that

347
00:22:31,660 --> 00:22:33,580
because I listened to other conversations

348
00:22:33,580 --> 00:22:34,700
regarding it at the time.

349
00:22:35,660 --> 00:22:37,940
But yes, I see what you

350
00:22:37,940 --> 00:22:40,220
mean now about analysis as such.

351
00:22:40,220 --> 00:22:40,940
It seems to me very clear.

352
00:22:40,940 --> 00:22:44,540
K. Analysis implies, sir, the analyser and the analysed.

353
00:22:44,540 --> 00:22:45,100
A. Precisely.

354
00:22:45,740 --> 00:22:47,900
K. The analyser is the analysed.

355
00:22:47,900 --> 00:22:51,020
And also analysis implies time, duration.

356
00:22:51,020 --> 00:22:57,340
I must take time to unearth, to uncover,

357
00:22:57,340 --> 00:22:59,740
and it takes me the rest of my life.

358
00:23:00,860 --> 00:23:03,020
A. This is a confusion we have about death too,

359
00:23:03,020 --> 00:23:04,700
death's relation to time.

360
00:23:04,700 --> 00:23:06,139
K. That's right. I'm coming to that.

361
00:23:06,139 --> 00:23:08,700
A. Yes, of course. Yes. Please do. Please.

362
00:23:08,700 --> 00:23:12,620
K. Yes. So, the

363
00:23:12,620 --> 00:23:16,540
mind perceiving discards analysis completely.

364
00:23:16,540 --> 00:23:19,740
Not because it's not profitable,

365
00:23:19,740 --> 00:23:22,139
not because it doesn't get me where I want,

366
00:23:22,139 --> 00:23:26,780
but I see the impossibility

367
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:30,620
of emptying the consciousness of its content

368
00:23:30,620 --> 00:23:36,060
if the mind approaches through that channel.

369
00:23:37,659 --> 00:23:42,300
Analyzer, time, and the utter futility

370
00:23:42,300 --> 00:23:46,700
and the utter futility at the end of forty years.

371
00:23:46,700 --> 00:23:48,060
I'm still analysing.

372
00:23:50,460 --> 00:23:52,300
A. And the content of my consciousness

373
00:23:52,300 --> 00:23:54,060
has not qualitatively changed.

374
00:23:54,060 --> 00:23:54,860
K. Changed at all.

375
00:23:54,860 --> 00:23:57,740
A. No, it's become intensified in its corruption.

376
00:23:57,740 --> 00:23:59,500
K. That's right.

377
00:23:59,500 --> 00:24:00,220
A. Yes.

378
00:24:00,220 --> 00:24:06,060
K. So, but the mind must see its content,

379
00:24:07,820 --> 00:24:10,220
must be totally aware of it,

380
00:24:10,220 --> 00:24:12,620
not fragments, fragments of it.

381
00:24:14,540 --> 00:24:15,660
How is that to be done?

382
00:24:17,260 --> 00:24:17,980
You follow, sir?

383
00:24:17,980 --> 00:24:19,020
A. Yes, I do.

384
00:24:19,020 --> 00:24:23,420
K. Because that's very important in relation to death.

385
00:24:25,820 --> 00:24:31,260
Because content of my consciousness is consciousness.

386
00:24:31,980 --> 00:24:36,860
That consciousness is me, my ego,

387
00:24:37,820 --> 00:24:43,659
my saying, I and you, we and they,

388
00:24:45,820 --> 00:24:48,540
whether they are the communists, they are the Catholics,

389
00:24:48,540 --> 00:24:51,500
they are the Protestants or the Hindus, they and we.

390
00:24:54,860 --> 00:24:58,060
So, it is very important to find out

391
00:24:59,659 --> 00:25:03,820
whether it's possible to empty consciousness of its content,

392
00:25:04,780 --> 00:25:08,460
which means the dying to the me.

393
00:25:12,060 --> 00:25:12,860
You follow?

394
00:25:12,860 --> 00:25:15,020
A. Yes, I do.

395
00:25:15,020 --> 00:25:16,139
K. Because that is the me.

396
00:25:19,419 --> 00:25:20,860
A. This is where the terror starts.

397
00:25:20,860 --> 00:25:22,220
K. That's where the terror starts.

398
00:25:22,220 --> 00:25:24,700
A. Precisely. There's the intuition that if I die

399
00:25:24,700 --> 00:25:27,419
to the content of this consciousness,

400
00:25:27,419 --> 00:25:28,780
that I am wiped out.

401
00:25:28,780 --> 00:25:31,420
I, who have worked,

402
00:25:32,300 --> 00:25:35,100
who have lived a righteous life or an unrighteous life,

403
00:25:35,740 --> 00:25:40,700
who have done so much mischief or good,

404
00:25:41,899 --> 00:25:44,060
I have struggled to better myself,

405
00:25:45,260 --> 00:25:47,340
I have been so kind,

406
00:25:47,340 --> 00:25:49,420
so gentle, so angry, so bitter.

407
00:25:50,700 --> 00:25:54,300
And when you say, empty your consciousness,

408
00:25:54,300 --> 00:25:57,420
it means you are asking me to better yourself.

409
00:25:57,420 --> 00:25:59,980
You are asking me to die to all that.

410
00:26:02,140 --> 00:26:06,860
So, you are touching at the very root of fear.

411
00:26:10,540 --> 00:26:11,820
A. Yes, exactly.

412
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:14,140
K. At the root of terror of not being.

413
00:26:19,340 --> 00:26:22,220
And – yes, that's it, sir.

414
00:26:22,780 --> 00:26:27,820
And I want to immortalise – that's me.

415
00:26:31,660 --> 00:26:34,380
I do it through books,

416
00:26:34,380 --> 00:26:36,620
writing a book and say, famous book.

417
00:26:39,180 --> 00:26:40,300
Or I paint.

418
00:26:43,020 --> 00:26:46,540
Or through paint, through works, through good acts,

419
00:26:46,540 --> 00:26:49,420
through building this or that,

420
00:26:49,420 --> 00:26:53,100
I immortalise myself.

421
00:26:55,660 --> 00:26:58,540
A. This has very pernicious effects within the family.

422
00:26:59,660 --> 00:27:01,100
Because we must have a son

423
00:27:02,300 --> 00:27:06,780
in order to immortalise the name in time.

424
00:27:06,780 --> 00:27:08,940
K. Therefore the family becomes a danger.

425
00:27:09,660 --> 00:27:10,220
A. Exactly.

426
00:27:15,100 --> 00:27:17,340
K. So, look what we have done, sir.

427
00:27:17,340 --> 00:27:21,419
The ancient Egyptians immortalised them, sir,

428
00:27:21,419 --> 00:27:25,260
made their life immortal by thinking, carrying on.

429
00:27:26,300 --> 00:27:27,260
A. Perpetuating.

430
00:27:27,260 --> 00:27:28,220
K. Perpetuating.

431
00:27:30,300 --> 00:27:34,620
And the robbers come and tear it all to pieces.

432
00:27:36,220 --> 00:27:39,580
Tutankhamun means merely a mask now,

433
00:27:39,580 --> 00:27:41,659
a golden mask with a mummy.

434
00:27:41,660 --> 00:27:43,260
A golden mask with a mummy.

435
00:27:44,220 --> 00:27:45,420
And so on.

436
00:27:45,420 --> 00:27:50,940
So, man has sought immortality through works,

437
00:27:50,940 --> 00:27:57,020
through every way to find that which is immortal.

438
00:27:58,540 --> 00:28:01,900
That is, beyond mortality.

439
00:28:04,140 --> 00:28:04,700
Right?

440
00:28:05,500 --> 00:28:07,900
A. It's a very remarkable thing that the word immortal

441
00:28:07,900 --> 00:28:08,860
is a negative.

442
00:28:08,860 --> 00:28:11,020
K. Negative, yes. Not mortal.

443
00:28:11,020 --> 00:28:13,660
A. Yes. It's not saying what it is.

444
00:28:17,900 --> 00:28:19,740
K. We are going to find out what it is.

445
00:28:19,740 --> 00:28:20,240
A. Good.

446
00:28:21,740 --> 00:28:23,660
K. You follow, sir, this is a very serious thing.

447
00:28:23,660 --> 00:28:26,700
It isn't a plaything between two people

448
00:28:26,700 --> 00:28:28,460
who are enjoying discussion,

449
00:28:28,460 --> 00:28:30,220
it's a tremendously important thing.

450
00:28:30,220 --> 00:28:32,379
A. Yes. I was laughing...

451
00:28:32,379 --> 00:28:33,260
K. Oh, I'm not...

452
00:28:34,700 --> 00:28:36,620
A. ...at the irony of it.

453
00:28:36,620 --> 00:28:40,540
That inherent in the structure of that word

454
00:28:40,540 --> 00:28:41,500
there is a warning,

455
00:28:42,300 --> 00:28:44,460
and we just go right through the red light.

456
00:28:44,460 --> 00:28:45,100
K. Right.

457
00:28:45,100 --> 00:28:47,100
A. Yes. Please, please go on.

458
00:28:47,100 --> 00:28:50,700
K. So, what is immortality?

459
00:28:52,460 --> 00:28:53,180
Not the book.

460
00:28:54,780 --> 00:28:55,420
A. Oh, no.

461
00:28:55,420 --> 00:28:57,500
K. Not the painting which I have done,

462
00:28:57,500 --> 00:28:59,620
not going to the moon and

463
00:28:59,620 --> 00:29:01,740
putting some idiotic flag up there.

464
00:29:03,659 --> 00:29:06,139
Not living a righteous life,

465
00:29:07,180 --> 00:29:08,700
or not living a righteous life.

466
00:29:09,580 --> 00:29:11,260
So, what is immortality?

467
00:29:15,580 --> 00:29:17,660
The cathedrals are beautiful,

468
00:29:19,020 --> 00:29:20,300
marvellous cathedrals,

469
00:29:21,180 --> 00:29:23,660
in stone, earthquake comes, gone.

470
00:29:25,820 --> 00:29:29,580
You build, you carve out of marble

471
00:29:29,580 --> 00:29:31,580
a marvellous thing of Michelangelo,

472
00:29:33,100 --> 00:29:34,780
earthquake, fire, destroyed,

473
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:36,700
some lunatic comes on with

474
00:29:36,700 --> 00:29:38,060
a hammer and breaks it up.

475
00:29:39,340 --> 00:29:42,860
So, it is in none of those.

476
00:29:44,620 --> 00:29:45,340
Right?

477
00:29:45,340 --> 00:29:45,900
A. Right.

478
00:29:45,900 --> 00:29:49,740
K. Because that is capable of being destroyed.

479
00:29:53,340 --> 00:29:56,380
Every statue becomes a dead thing,

480
00:29:59,020 --> 00:30:00,860
every poem, every painting.

481
00:30:03,020 --> 00:30:05,980
So, then one asks, what is immortality?

482
00:30:05,980 --> 00:30:07,420
It's not in the building,

483
00:30:07,420 --> 00:30:08,300
not in the building.

484
00:30:09,020 --> 00:30:10,300
Just see it, sir.

485
00:30:10,300 --> 00:30:11,660
It's not in the cathedral,

486
00:30:12,220 --> 00:30:16,220
it's not in the saviour which you have invented,

487
00:30:17,820 --> 00:30:19,740
which thought has invented,

488
00:30:19,740 --> 00:30:21,500
not in the gods that man

489
00:30:21,500 --> 00:30:23,260
has created out of his own image.

490
00:30:25,420 --> 00:30:26,780
Then what is immortality?

491
00:30:29,260 --> 00:30:33,500
Because that is related to consciousness and to death.

492
00:30:34,300 --> 00:30:37,900
Unless I find that out, death is a terror.

493
00:30:38,780 --> 00:30:39,900
A. Of course.

494
00:30:41,100 --> 00:30:41,900
Of course.

495
00:30:41,900 --> 00:30:45,100
K. I have tried to immortalise myself,

496
00:30:45,100 --> 00:30:50,460
become immortal by the thought that there is a Brahman,

497
00:30:50,460 --> 00:30:52,860
there is a God, there is eternity,

498
00:30:52,860 --> 00:30:55,980
there is a nameless one,

499
00:30:55,980 --> 00:30:59,900
and I will do everything to approach him.

500
00:31:00,140 --> 00:31:02,860
I will do everything to approach him,

501
00:31:04,300 --> 00:31:05,980
therefore I will lead a righteous life,

502
00:31:07,180 --> 00:31:10,380
therefore I will pray, I will beg, I will obey,

503
00:31:11,020 --> 00:31:15,420
I will live a life of poverty, chastity,

504
00:31:15,420 --> 00:31:16,860
and so on, so on, so on,

505
00:31:18,460 --> 00:31:23,180
in order to have that immortal reality with me.

506
00:31:24,620 --> 00:31:28,700
But I know all that is the born of thought.

507
00:31:30,700 --> 00:31:31,500
Right, sir?

508
00:31:31,500 --> 00:31:32,060
A. Yes.

509
00:31:32,060 --> 00:31:33,500
K. Wait, sir. See what happens.

510
00:31:34,780 --> 00:31:39,100
So I see thought and its products

511
00:31:39,100 --> 00:31:40,780
are the children of barren women.

512
00:31:42,620 --> 00:31:43,260
A. Precisely.

513
00:31:44,940 --> 00:31:46,380
K. See what is taking place.

514
00:31:46,380 --> 00:31:47,980
Then what is immortality?

515
00:31:48,540 --> 00:31:48,940
Right.

516
00:31:58,060 --> 00:32:02,240
The beauty in the Church, not I built the Church.

517
00:32:03,180 --> 00:32:06,380
The beauty in the Cathedral, the beauty in the poem,

518
00:32:06,380 --> 00:32:09,260
the beauty in the sculpture.

519
00:32:10,780 --> 00:32:11,900
The beauty.

520
00:32:13,420 --> 00:32:15,420
Not the object of beauty.

521
00:32:15,420 --> 00:32:16,060
A. Not the object.

522
00:32:16,060 --> 00:32:19,860
K. The beauty itself.

523
00:32:19,860 --> 00:32:22,860
That is immortal.

524
00:32:22,860 --> 00:32:25,940
And I cannot grasp that,

525
00:32:25,940 --> 00:32:28,460
the mind cannot grasp it,

526
00:32:28,460 --> 00:32:36,620
because beauty is not in the field of consciousness.

527
00:32:39,460 --> 00:32:41,540
A. You see, what you've said, again,

528
00:32:41,540 --> 00:32:44,379
stands it all on its head.

529
00:32:44,380 --> 00:32:46,900
We think when something dies

530
00:32:46,900 --> 00:32:50,020
that we have cherished, that it is beautiful,

531
00:32:50,020 --> 00:32:54,620
that beauty dies in some sense

532
00:32:54,620 --> 00:33:00,380
with that which has passed away.

533
00:33:00,380 --> 00:33:08,340
Actually, it's the feeling of being bereft of that beauty

534
00:33:08,340 --> 00:33:11,180
that I regarded as my privilege

535
00:33:11,180 --> 00:33:14,060
to have personal access to,

536
00:33:14,060 --> 00:33:17,460
the belief that that has perished,

537
00:33:17,460 --> 00:33:20,020
not simply been lost,

538
00:33:20,020 --> 00:33:25,220
because what is lost is, by its nature,

539
00:33:25,220 --> 00:33:27,220
predisposed to be found,

540
00:33:27,220 --> 00:33:30,040
but to perish is to

541
00:33:30,040 --> 00:33:32,860
be wiped out utterly, isn't it?

542
00:33:32,860 --> 00:33:35,460
And so the belief is deep.

543
00:33:35,460 --> 00:33:36,820
K. Oh, very, very.

544
00:33:36,820 --> 00:33:38,479
A. Extremely deep with respect

545
00:33:38,479 --> 00:33:40,139
to what we mean by perish.

546
00:33:40,139 --> 00:33:43,020
In fact, the word isn't used very often, it's frightening.

547
00:33:43,060 --> 00:33:43,940
It's a very frightening word.

548
00:33:43,940 --> 00:33:45,460
We always talk about losing things.

549
00:33:45,460 --> 00:33:48,940
Hardly ever do we say something perishes.

550
00:33:48,940 --> 00:33:51,240
Now, back to what I mentioned

551
00:33:51,240 --> 00:33:53,540
about standing it on its head.

552
00:33:53,540 --> 00:34:00,420
The image came to my mind as a metaphor,

553
00:34:00,420 --> 00:34:02,240
I hope not one of

554
00:34:02,240 --> 00:34:04,060
those images we've been talking about,

555
00:34:04,060 --> 00:34:10,940
that beauty, rather than being imprisoned

556
00:34:10,940 --> 00:34:16,739
and therefore taken down to the utter depths of nullity

557
00:34:16,739 --> 00:34:19,380
when the thing perishes,

558
00:34:19,380 --> 00:34:24,179
has simply let it go.

559
00:34:24,179 --> 00:34:30,179
In some sense, beauty has let this expression go.

560
00:34:30,179 --> 00:34:33,500
That is upside down from what is usually thought.

561
00:34:33,500 --> 00:34:36,219
K. I know, I know.

562
00:34:36,219 --> 00:34:41,899
And it's probably let it go precisely on time.

563
00:34:41,899 --> 00:34:45,859
That's what's so marvellous. Yes.

564
00:34:45,859 --> 00:34:50,059
So, immortality, we have said,

565
00:34:50,059 --> 00:34:54,259
is within the field of time.

566
00:34:55,580 --> 00:34:58,259
A. The one field.

567
00:34:58,259 --> 00:34:59,339
K. Right? A. Yes.

568
00:34:59,339 --> 00:35:01,779
K. The field of time.

569
00:35:01,780 --> 00:35:06,100
And death is also then in the field of time.

570
00:35:06,100 --> 00:35:15,540
Because I have created through thought the things of time.

571
00:35:15,540 --> 00:35:20,580
And death is the ending or the

572
00:35:20,580 --> 00:35:25,620
beginning of a state which is timeless.

573
00:35:25,620 --> 00:35:29,700
Of that I am frightened.

574
00:35:29,700 --> 00:35:38,060
So, I want everything preserved in the field of time.

575
00:35:40,060 --> 00:35:42,140
You follow, sir? A. Yes, we think it could be.

576
00:35:42,140 --> 00:35:46,180
K. And that is what we call immortal.

577
00:35:46,180 --> 00:35:51,540
The statue, the poem, the church, the cathedral.

578
00:35:51,540 --> 00:35:57,980
And I see also all that is corruptible, destroyed

579
00:35:57,980 --> 00:36:02,580
by one accident or by an earthquake.

580
00:36:02,580 --> 00:36:06,540
Everything is gone.

581
00:36:06,540 --> 00:36:17,100
So, immortality is not within the field of time.

582
00:36:17,100 --> 00:36:22,300
And time is thought.

583
00:36:22,300 --> 00:36:24,380
A. Of course. Yes, that follows.

584
00:36:24,380 --> 00:36:30,100
K. Of course. So, anything that thought creates

585
00:36:30,100 --> 00:36:36,100
must be within the field of time.

586
00:36:36,100 --> 00:36:40,700
And yet thought is trying to seek immortality,

587
00:36:40,700 --> 00:36:45,420
which is immortality of itself

588
00:36:45,420 --> 00:36:50,140
and the things it has created.

589
00:36:50,140 --> 00:36:51,740
You see, you...

590
00:36:51,740 --> 00:36:57,299
So, then the problem is,

591
00:36:57,299 --> 00:37:02,859
can the mind see all this?

592
00:37:02,859 --> 00:37:08,060
See it, not imagine that it is seeing it.

593
00:37:08,060 --> 00:37:12,700
A. No, actually see it.

594
00:37:12,700 --> 00:37:16,779
Yes, the remark I made before,

595
00:37:16,779 --> 00:37:18,940
when you began saying the field of time,

596
00:37:18,940 --> 00:37:21,260
and I said the one field,

597
00:37:21,260 --> 00:37:23,980
I didn't mean that the field of time,

598
00:37:23,980 --> 00:37:25,820
as you have described it, is the one field,

599
00:37:25,820 --> 00:37:30,740
but that we could be so appallingly mistaken and blind...

600
00:37:30,740 --> 00:37:31,820
K. ...ignorant.

601
00:37:31,820 --> 00:37:36,020
A. ...that the field of time is another fragment

602
00:37:36,020 --> 00:37:38,940
and it is the only field.

603
00:37:38,940 --> 00:37:48,220
And what really struck me was this misuse of thought

604
00:37:48,220 --> 00:37:51,339
generates the most appalling avarice.

605
00:37:51,339 --> 00:37:54,540
K. Yes, sir.

606
00:37:54,540 --> 00:38:02,459
A. It's... I'm walling myself up in stone.

607
00:38:02,459 --> 00:38:03,859
Yes, please.

608
00:38:03,859 --> 00:38:12,779
K. So, the mind perceiving all this,

609
00:38:12,779 --> 00:38:15,020
if it is alert, if it has been watchful,

610
00:38:15,020 --> 00:38:19,740
all the time that we have been discussing,

611
00:38:19,740 --> 00:38:27,180
it must inevitably see the whole content exposed

612
00:38:27,180 --> 00:38:29,620
without any effort.

613
00:38:29,620 --> 00:38:31,580
It's like reading a map.

614
00:38:31,580 --> 00:38:35,820
You spread it out and look.

615
00:38:35,820 --> 00:38:38,780
But if you want to go in a direction,

616
00:38:38,780 --> 00:38:43,380
then you don't look at the whole map.

617
00:38:43,380 --> 00:38:44,400
Then you say, I want

618
00:38:44,400 --> 00:38:45,420
to go from here to there,

619
00:38:45,420 --> 00:38:47,220
the direction is there so many miles,

620
00:38:47,220 --> 00:38:51,740
and you don't look the rest.

621
00:38:51,740 --> 00:38:58,820
What we are asking is, no direction, but just look.

622
00:38:58,820 --> 00:39:03,340
Look at the content of your consciousness

623
00:39:03,340 --> 00:39:09,260
without direction, without choice.

624
00:39:09,260 --> 00:39:18,300
Be aware of it without any exertion of discernment.

625
00:39:18,300 --> 00:39:26,540
Be choicelessly aware of this extraordinary map.

626
00:39:26,540 --> 00:39:29,220
Then that choiceless awareness

627
00:39:29,220 --> 00:39:34,020
gives you the tremendous energy to go beyond it.

628
00:39:34,020 --> 00:39:39,100
But you need energy to go beyond it.

629
00:39:39,100 --> 00:39:46,460
A. This leads me to the notion of reincarnation

630
00:39:46,460 --> 00:39:48,940
that we began to touch on a little earlier.

631
00:39:48,940 --> 00:39:54,340
I see the demonic root in that.

632
00:39:54,340 --> 00:39:59,980
K. You see, reincarnate next life.

633
00:39:59,980 --> 00:40:02,940
Nobody says, incarnate now.

634
00:40:02,940 --> 00:40:04,220
A. Yes, exactly.

635
00:40:04,220 --> 00:40:06,220
K. You follow, sir? A. Yes, I do.

636
00:40:06,220 --> 00:40:09,660
K. You can only incarnate now

637
00:40:09,660 --> 00:40:13,100
when you die to the content.

638
00:40:13,100 --> 00:40:17,660
You can be reborn, regenerated totally

639
00:40:17,660 --> 00:40:21,940
if you die to the content.

640
00:40:21,980 --> 00:40:23,500
Yes, yes.

641
00:40:23,500 --> 00:40:31,700
And there is a terrible truth on the dark side,

642
00:40:31,700 --> 00:40:35,940
the demonic side, to this doctrine of reincarnation,

643
00:40:35,940 --> 00:40:38,900
because if that content of consciousness

644
00:40:38,900 --> 00:40:43,780
is not emptied out, then it must prevail.

645
00:40:43,780 --> 00:40:44,940
K. So what happens?

646
00:40:44,940 --> 00:40:47,420
A. Then it really does. Yes.

647
00:40:47,500 --> 00:40:52,260
K. It prevails. So what happens?

648
00:40:52,260 --> 00:40:54,880
I do not know, as a

649
00:40:54,880 --> 00:40:57,500
human being, how to empty this thing.

650
00:40:57,500 --> 00:41:01,300
I am not even interested. I am only frightened.

651
00:41:01,300 --> 00:41:03,740
A. Only scared to death. K. Scared to death.

652
00:41:03,740 --> 00:41:07,100
And I preserve something, and I die, I am burnt,

653
00:41:07,100 --> 00:41:10,780
or buried underground.

654
00:41:10,780 --> 00:41:15,620
The content goes on.

655
00:41:15,620 --> 00:41:19,120
As we said, the content

656
00:41:19,120 --> 00:41:22,620
of me is your content also.

657
00:41:22,620 --> 00:41:24,339
It is not so very different.

658
00:41:24,339 --> 00:41:27,060
No, no, no, no.

659
00:41:27,060 --> 00:41:30,020
Slightly modified, slightly exaggerated,

660
00:41:30,020 --> 00:41:32,779
given certain tendencies which depend on

661
00:41:32,779 --> 00:41:35,620
your conditioning of environment, so on, so on.

662
00:41:35,620 --> 00:41:41,700
But it is essentially the same consciousness.

663
00:41:41,700 --> 00:41:45,299
Unless a human being empties that consciousness,

664
00:41:45,300 --> 00:41:51,260
that consciousness goes on like a river,

665
00:41:51,260 --> 00:41:55,180
collecting, accumulating, all that is going on.

666
00:41:55,180 --> 00:42:00,940
And out of that river comes the expression

667
00:42:00,940 --> 00:42:06,700
or the manifestation of the one that is lost,

668
00:42:06,700 --> 00:42:12,980
when the mediums, seances, all those say,

669
00:42:12,980 --> 00:42:16,940
say, your brother, your uncle, your wife is here,

670
00:42:16,940 --> 00:42:21,380
what has happened is they have manifested themselves

671
00:42:21,380 --> 00:42:27,220
out of that stream which is the continuous consciousness

672
00:42:27,220 --> 00:42:36,420
of struggle, pain, unhappiness, all that.

673
00:42:36,420 --> 00:42:41,300
And a man who has observed

674
00:42:41,300 --> 00:42:45,500
and has looked at the consciousness and empties it,

675
00:42:45,500 --> 00:42:52,500
he doesn't belong to that stream at all.

676
00:42:52,500 --> 00:42:58,700
Then he is living each moment anew,

677
00:42:58,700 --> 00:43:01,940
because he is dying each moment. You understand?

678
00:43:01,940 --> 00:43:03,900
A.S. – Oh yes, I do.

679
00:43:03,900 --> 00:43:07,700
K. – There is no accumulation of the me

680
00:43:07,700 --> 00:43:13,700
which has to be expressed. He is dying every minute,

681
00:43:13,700 --> 00:43:16,899
living every minute and dying every minute.

682
00:43:16,899 --> 00:43:18,999
And therefore in that there is

683
00:43:18,999 --> 00:43:21,100
– what shall I say? –

684
00:43:21,100 --> 00:43:25,500
there is no content. You follow, sir?

685
00:43:25,500 --> 00:43:31,060
It is like a tremendous energy in action.

686
00:43:31,060 --> 00:43:34,500
A.S. – This gives a totally different understanding

687
00:43:34,500 --> 00:43:44,900
of what we mean by the phrase, in the afterlife.

688
00:43:44,900 --> 00:43:49,700
On the one hand, there is this continuity

689
00:43:49,700 --> 00:43:52,700
in disordered content of consciousness,

690
00:43:52,700 --> 00:43:54,900
K. It is totally disordered. That's right.

691
00:43:54,900 --> 00:43:59,900
A.S. – which is not radically affected, qualitatively,

692
00:43:59,900 --> 00:44:01,700
with respect to its nature,

693
00:44:01,700 --> 00:44:05,299
simply because somebody has stopped breathing for good.

694
00:44:05,299 --> 00:44:07,700
No, it's on its way.

695
00:44:07,700 --> 00:44:16,899
And therefore the attempt that is often made

696
00:44:16,899 --> 00:44:19,499
on the part of persons

697
00:44:19,499 --> 00:44:22,100
to contact this stream of consciousness

698
00:44:22,100 --> 00:44:25,100
after the death of a person,

699
00:44:25,100 --> 00:44:31,500
when made within the same quality of consciousness,

700
00:44:31,500 --> 00:44:35,100
attains nothing but a reinforcement

701
00:44:35,100 --> 00:44:37,100
within their own personal life,

702
00:44:37,100 --> 00:44:38,700
and it does a terrible

703
00:44:38,700 --> 00:44:40,300
thing to that content of consciousness

704
00:44:40,300 --> 00:44:42,300
which has gone on, since

705
00:44:42,300 --> 00:44:44,300
it also feeds that some more.

706
00:44:44,300 --> 00:44:47,900
K. That's right. Yes, I do see that.

707
00:44:47,900 --> 00:44:52,000
K. A person came to see

708
00:44:52,000 --> 00:44:56,100
me, and his wife was dead,

709
00:44:56,100 --> 00:44:59,500
and he really thought he loved her.

710
00:44:59,500 --> 00:45:03,500
So he said, I must see my wife again.

711
00:45:03,500 --> 00:45:05,700
Can you help me?

712
00:45:05,700 --> 00:45:08,900
I said, which wife do you want to see?

713
00:45:08,900 --> 00:45:11,500
The one that cooked?

714
00:45:11,500 --> 00:45:13,700
The one that bore the children?

715
00:45:13,700 --> 00:45:16,700
The one that gave you sex?

716
00:45:16,700 --> 00:45:19,900
The one that quarrelled with you?

717
00:45:19,900 --> 00:45:24,500
The one that dominated you, frightened you?

718
00:45:25,700 --> 00:45:27,900
He said, I don't want to meet any of those.

719
00:45:27,900 --> 00:45:31,900
I want to meet the good of her.

720
00:45:35,300 --> 00:45:37,300
You follow, sir?

721
00:45:37,300 --> 00:45:40,300
The image of the good

722
00:45:40,300 --> 00:45:43,300
he has built out of her.

723
00:45:43,300 --> 00:45:46,100
None of the ugly things,

724
00:45:46,100 --> 00:45:47,900
or what he considered ugly things,

725
00:45:47,900 --> 00:45:51,200
but the idea of the good

726
00:45:51,200 --> 00:45:54,500
which he had culled out of her,

727
00:45:54,500 --> 00:45:56,500
and that is the image he wants to meet.

728
00:45:56,500 --> 00:46:00,500
I said, don't be infantile.

729
00:46:01,300 --> 00:46:03,300
You are so utterly immature

730
00:46:03,300 --> 00:46:05,200
when you have slept with

731
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:07,100
her, and got angry with her.

732
00:46:07,100 --> 00:46:08,300
All that you don't want,

733
00:46:08,300 --> 00:46:10,300
you want just the image

734
00:46:10,300 --> 00:46:12,300
which you have about her goodness.

735
00:46:12,300 --> 00:46:17,500
I said, and you know, sir, he began to cry,

736
00:46:17,500 --> 00:46:20,100
really cry for the first time.

737
00:46:20,100 --> 00:46:24,100
He said, afterwards I have cried when she died,

738
00:46:24,100 --> 00:46:29,100
but the tears were of self-pity, my loneliness,

739
00:46:29,500 --> 00:46:34,900
my sense of inertia, you follow, lack of things.

740
00:46:34,900 --> 00:46:37,800
Now I am crying, I have cried

741
00:46:37,800 --> 00:46:40,700
because I see what I have done.

742
00:46:40,700 --> 00:46:43,500
You understand, sir?

743
00:46:43,500 --> 00:46:47,500
A. Yes, I do.

744
00:46:47,500 --> 00:46:54,500
So, to understand death there must be no fear.

745
00:46:54,500 --> 00:46:57,500
The fear exists and the terror of it exists

746
00:46:57,500 --> 00:47:04,500
only when the content is not understood.

747
00:47:04,500 --> 00:47:10,500
And the content is the me.

748
00:47:10,500 --> 00:47:15,500
He is the me.

749
00:47:15,500 --> 00:47:20,500
And the me is the chair. You follow, sir?

750
00:47:20,500 --> 00:47:25,500
The thing I am attached to. It is so stupid.

751
00:47:25,500 --> 00:47:29,500
And I am frightened of that.

752
00:47:29,500 --> 00:47:34,500
The bank account, the family, you follow?

753
00:47:34,500 --> 00:47:38,500
A. Oh yes, yes I do.

754
00:47:38,500 --> 00:47:44,500
K. Unless one is really deeply serious in this matter,

755
00:47:44,500 --> 00:47:49,500
you can't incarnate now,

756
00:47:49,500 --> 00:47:52,500
in the deep sense of that word,

757
00:47:52,500 --> 00:47:56,500
and therefore immortality is in the book,

758
00:47:56,500 --> 00:47:58,500
in the statue, in the cathedral,

759
00:47:58,500 --> 00:48:04,500
in the things I have put together by thought.

760
00:48:04,500 --> 00:48:07,500
That is all field of time.

761
00:48:07,500 --> 00:48:11,500
A. Right. It just occurred to me

762
00:48:11,500 --> 00:48:15,500
what a terrible thing we have been doing

763
00:48:15,500 --> 00:48:21,500
so often over and over again to Plato.

764
00:48:21,500 --> 00:48:27,500
By this perennial attempt, academic analysis of the text,

765
00:48:27,500 --> 00:48:32,500
when he plainly said that the business of the philosopher,

766
00:48:32,500 --> 00:48:34,500
by which he didn't mean the analyser

767
00:48:34,500 --> 00:48:37,500
in this mad way that we

768
00:48:37,500 --> 00:48:40,500
have been observing, it goes on,

769
00:48:40,500 --> 00:48:42,500
the business of the philosopher,

770
00:48:42,500 --> 00:48:45,500
namely the one who is concerned

771
00:48:45,500 --> 00:48:48,500
with a radical change in rebirth,

772
00:48:48,500 --> 00:48:50,500
which he associates with wisdom,

773
00:48:50,500 --> 00:48:56,500
the business of the philosopher is to practise dying.

774
00:48:56,500 --> 00:48:59,500
To practise dying.

775
00:48:59,500 --> 00:49:03,500
Yes, I don't think he meant routine,

776
00:49:03,500 --> 00:49:07,500
repetition of die, die, die, die, die.

777
00:49:07,500 --> 00:49:11,500
I think he puts it with an ing,

778
00:49:11,500 --> 00:49:18,500
because he doesn't want to fall out of act.

779
00:49:18,500 --> 00:49:20,500
I know I use this phrase all the time,

780
00:49:20,500 --> 00:49:22,500
but it came to me early in our conversations,

781
00:49:22,500 --> 00:49:25,500
and it seems to say for

782
00:49:25,500 --> 00:49:28,500
me what I want to say.

783
00:49:28,500 --> 00:49:30,500
I have to say I learned it from you,

784
00:49:30,500 --> 00:49:33,000
though I don't want to

785
00:49:33,000 --> 00:49:35,500
put the words in your mouth.

786
00:49:35,500 --> 00:49:39,500
But it's possible to fall out of act

787
00:49:39,500 --> 00:49:44,500
into the terror and the demonic stream of time,

788
00:49:44,500 --> 00:49:47,500
but when one is in act,

789
00:49:47,500 --> 00:49:50,500
the whole thing is an ongoing movement.

790
00:49:50,500 --> 00:49:54,500
K. So, sir, time has a stop. A. Precisely.

791
00:49:54,500 --> 00:49:56,500
See the beauty of it, sir.

792
00:49:56,500 --> 00:50:00,500
And it is that beauty which is immortal,

793
00:50:00,500 --> 00:50:04,500
not the things which thought has created.

794
00:50:04,500 --> 00:50:07,500
A. Right.

795
00:50:07,500 --> 00:50:12,500
K. So, living is dying.

796
00:50:12,500 --> 00:50:14,500
A. Right.

797
00:50:14,500 --> 00:50:20,500
K. And love is essentially dying to the mean.

798
00:50:20,500 --> 00:50:28,500
Not the things which thought has said, this is love.

799
00:50:28,500 --> 00:50:32,500
Love, sex, love, pleasure, you follow? All that.

800
00:50:32,500 --> 00:50:39,500
It is the dying to time is love.

801
00:50:39,500 --> 00:50:48,500
